  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased maize value chain efficiency in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the value chain of maize in Rwanda.The maize currently produced, contains high levels of aflatoxin contamination, which poses a threat to consumer health. The project will contribute to the elimination of aflatoxin from Rwanda&apos;s maize value chain by making the post-harvest part of the value chain more efficient.As a result, the postharvest losses will decrease, the nutritional value of the maize will be improved and the incomes of 30,000 farmers will be increased by 56% due to the higher value and prices of the maize.</narrative>
  </description>
